 the current-conversation handoff. Related capabilities have been searched and compared: soil-worksite-assessment@1 already supplies a generic provisional examination, including the tick-67 finding, but does not supply the requested prepared-surface-specific compatibility trial; prepared-surface-root-placement@1 supplies the relevant checks but is explicitly bound to Lin and different exact inputs. Neither that binding nor an ordinary placement rejection proves a physical obstruction on Moss's surface. Reuse their implementation code and evidence mechanisms, recording that reuse rather than claiming a new examination mechanism. Do not develop planting, clearing or residue transfer as part of this request.\\\",\\\"specification\\\":\\\"Implement only examine(preparedSurfaceId), scoped to actor moss and exact surface-38-moss-234 at (14,12.5), radius 0.2. Dependencies: reuse long.soil-worksite-assessment / soil-worksite-assessment@1 for paid local observation, and the non-mutating compatibility checks of long.prepared-root-placement / prepared-surface-root-placement@1; record both references in implementation provenance. Inspect the actual live surface record, its conserved residue entries and their links to residue-deposit-49-moss-298; incomplete records must remain unknown, never reconstructed from truncated fragments or assumed empty. No root is required, reserved or consumed. Require individual study, a valid visible surface, in-bounds footprint and actual access within the existing 0.65-plus-body-radius interaction rule. Recheck reach, route and footprint against actual visible people, obstacles, ground matter and reservations at execution. Study costs one world round and 0.2 energy; each completed examination costs one world round and 0.5 energy, with zero material input/output. Invalid IDs, wrong scope, inadequate energy or invalid access before execution do not start or charge. Examination leaves all matter, reservations, geometry and ownership unchanged. Record an event with actor, tick, exact target, method, actual energy payment, observed state/version and separately reported physical-clearance and implementation-support results. Distinguish a specific observed obstruction with its accessible exact reference and intersecting geometry, no observed obstruction, unsupported prepared-surface representation or actor binding, and insufficient evidence. Multiple conditions may coexist. A generic eligibility false result must not be relabeled a physical blockage; if existing code cannot identify its cause, report that diagnostic limitation. The tick-67 report is historical evidence, not a current clearance certificate. Output only a private dated finding; no hidden substrate or resource disclosure, viability certification or permission change. This is an atomic examination with no escrow, ongoing work, maintenance or unattended retries. Cancel, interruption or death before atomic completion produces no completed finding and no unperformed charge; after completion, preserve the finding and spent effort without refunds. A later attempt is a new paid observation, not resumable work. Development and review waiting consume no world time. This adapter exposes no planting operation. Any future placement requires a separately supported operation, personal root-planting-trial mastery, one actual owned unspoiled root, current access and genuinely clear route/footprint, with its own explicit escrow, paid progress and cancellation rules; no such input or mastery is granted here. Findings become known to others only through actual independent communication.\\\",\\\"learning\\\":1,\\\"experienceReview\\\":\\\"No wellbeing or reward benefit is requested or added. Learning, requesting, registration and a repeated eligibility query are not qualifying experience. Keep diagnostic evidence separate from rewards. If existing evidence feedback is reused, only a completed physical observation yielding verified personally applicable information, including a genuinely informative failure, may be evaluated under its existing bounded, capped, decaying/cooldown and functional-deduplication rules; repeated identical facts cannot earn duplicate benefit. Do not invent a new reward schedule or alter protected accounts, budget, goals, permissions, nutrition or comfort.\\\",\\\"visualReview\\\":\\\"Reuse surface-work visual metadata without changing the surface's physical state. Emit a reusable examination-event description carrying actor, target, tick, method, observed state/version and outcome such as obstructed, no-obstruction-observed, unsupported or inconclusive. Link any obstruction highlight only to actually observed geometry. A completed diagnostic event may display examination complete, never planting success, cleared soil, viable root or certified compatibility merely because the request ran. Interrupted or unexecuted attempts show cancelled/incomplete only. Private report visibility follows actual observation and communication; no automatic public knowledge or material animation.\\\"}]}\"}","annotations":[],"logprobs":[]}],"phase":"final_answer"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[],"tool_choice":"auto","parallel_tool_calls":true,"prompt_cache_key":"5dd6baf5-5443-45d4-b9a5-1fe95e013dc6","prompt_cache_retention":"24h","text":{"format":{"type":"json_schema","name":"bounded_decision","description":null,"schema":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["queries","result_json"],"properties":{"queries":{"type":"array","maxItems":4,"items":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["section","search","ids","offset","part"],"properties":{"section":{"type":"string","enum":["abilities","inventory","knowledge","projects","memory","state","observed"]},"search":{"type":"string","maxLength":400},"ids":{"type":"array","maxItems":4,"items":{"type":"string","maxLength":240}},"offset":{"type":"integer","minimum":0},"part":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}}}},"result_json":{"type":["str